                 template resolves to — UI-Panel-Button-{Up,Down,Highlight} (all verified in the MPQ),
                 stretched over the button as its Normal/Pushed/Highlight art. The "Goodbye" label
                 (GlobalStrings GOODBYE = "Goodbye") is an OVERLAY FontString centred on the button (the
                 real ButtonText draws in the OVERLAY layer). Wired to the same close path as the close
                 button (CloseGossip → HideUIPanel), mirroring the ref's OnClick HideUIPanel(GossipFrame). -->
        </Frames>
        <Scripts>
            <OnLoad>GossipFrame_OnLoad()</OnLoad>
            <OnEvent>GossipFrame_OnEvent()</OnEvent>
            <!-- The row auto-height's settle pass (see BenillaGossipRow_Resize): our text measure
                 is a frame late, so the fit re-runs here until every visible row's label measure
                 lands. Fires only while the window is effectively visible. -->
            <OnUpdate>BenillaGossipFrame_OnUpdate()</OnUpdate>
            <!-- OnShow/OnHide, quoted from the real GossipFrame.xml frame Scripts (l.445/454): the
                 kits igQuestListOpen/Close, and — load-bearing — CloseGossip() on hide (the real
                 GossipFrame_OnHide). CloseGossip ends the gossip session whenever the frame hides,
                 INCLUDING when another NPC window displaces it at the UIPanel slot (SetLeftFrame →
                 oldFrame:Hide() → OnHide); without it the GossipState resource stayed set after a
                 vendor/quest window replaced the menu, and gossip would not reopen until the
                 range-guard reset it (decision 0095). No-packet client-side clear; idempotent with the
                 close button, which also calls it. Never fires at load (hidden="true"). -->
            <OnShow>PlaySound("igQuestListOpen")</OnShow>
            <OnHide>CloseGossip(); PlaySound("igQuestListClose")</OnHide>
        </Scripts>
